{
  "description": "The modifyHeaders golden fixture, read by both differential harnesses (src/core/blocking/__tests__/indexDifferential.test.ts and android/.../IndexDifferentialTest.kt): the same rule sets and probes, the same expected decisions – action, matched rule, request and response header edits in order, needsHeaders – so the two engines produce the same edits for the same rules. Requests are decided at the request stage; a probe with responseHeaders is decided again at the headers-received stage with them, as the desktop's onHeadersReceived and the Android relay decide. The first ext: set is User-Agent Switcher for Chrome's session rule as its background registers it (every resource type, no URL condition); ext:bbbb… is a newer extension (the higher slot of the band, contract 1.3), ext:aaaa… an older one.",
